<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theseus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theseus was a legendary king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> in Greek mythology, son of Aegeus, or of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poseidon">Poseidon</a>, and of Aethra of Troezen. Myths credit him with killing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minotaur">Minotaur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> and with the synoecism, the union of the villages of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a> under Athens. Classical Athenians honoured him as a founder of their state, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimon">Cimon</a> brought his supposed bones home from Skyros.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theseus.jpg" alt="Theseus" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aison · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kylix_Theseus_Aison_MNA_Inv11365_n1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
